# SPA fallback for client-side routes. Written as explicit routes rather
# than a `/*` wildcard because Cloudflare Pages currently has a false-positive
# "infinite loop" detector on wildcard rules whose target also falls under
# the wildcard's own pattern (e.g. `/* /index.html 200`) — see
# https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/issues/11824. It silently drops
# the rule rather than failing the build, so direct loads/refreshes of any
# route below would 404 without this. Add a line here whenever a new route
# is added to NAV_ITEMS / <Routes> in src/App.jsx.
/reminders   /index.html   200
/tasks       /index.html   200
/focus       /index.html   200
/braindump   /index.html   200
/habits      /index.html   200
/stats       /index.html   200
/calendar    /index.html   200
/settings    /index.html   200
